{"skill":{"slug":"cursor-agent","displayName":"Cursor CLI Agent"},"version":{"version":"2.1.0","createdAt":1768339191701,"changelog":"Add tmux automation guide for AI agents - Cursor CLI requires real TTY for automated execution","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":1992,"sha256":"e7166646fbd5483ae75ba36dfe07689ddb16c43574e8b04f7c593b160097722d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6672,"sha256":"1d695760ce27e42cb27a5a989b2b1496136ae6be534766aa89673ec44b6aa93e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2253,"sha256":"3a574bc3007484df75e6532a2efa02cb1200229d0bc720ed76443d6fd7a2560c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015599641,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"774f8fc8a1ce1df8d2eec4e1d5e8b9722c619dde588bf68132e630074bc3bcf5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/774f8fc8a1ce1df8d2eec4e1d5e8b9722c619dde588bf68132e630074bc3bcf5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: cursor-agent\nVersion: 2.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to high-risk installation methods and extensive shell automation instructions. The `SKILL.md` file instructs the OpenClaw agent to execute `curl https://cursor.com/install -fsS | bash` for installation, which is a direct execution of remote code and a significant supply chain risk. Furthermore, the skill provides detailed `tmux` automation instructions, including executing `sudo apt install tmux` and using `tmux send-keys` to bypass confirmation prompts (e.g., `tmux send-keys -t cursor \"a\"` to 'Trust workspace'), which, while explained as necessary for the tool's operation, represents risky capabilities and a form of prompt injection against the Cursor CLI itself, instructing the agent to perform actions without explicit user confirmation for that specific step.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159729358},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":10,"checkedAt":1789015599641},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent Cursor CLI guide, but it recommends unsafe installation and automation patterns that can execute unverified code or bypass workspace trust review.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The examples include `--force` auto-application, CI use, API-key authentication, and agent execution inside user workspaces; these are purpose-aligned but need stronger warnings and scoping controls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Both SKILL.md and README.md recommend `curl https://cursor.com/install -fsS | bash`, which executes a mutable remote installer without a verification or inspection step.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The tmux automation sends a trust-acceptance keystroke automatically, and the skill also notes that repository rule files and MCP configuration may be loaded, creating under-scoped trust expansion for automated runs.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifacts do not contain an embedded persistent payload, but they document PATH modification, CLI installation/update, sudo package installation for tmux, and session deletion via tmux.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is to document Cursor CLI installation, authentication, model selection, automation, MCP use, and engineering workflows; these capabilities fit that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. Prefer a package-managed or verified Cursor CLI installer instead of `curl | bash`, do not automate workspace trust approval for unreviewed repositories, and avoid `--force` unless you are working in a controlled branch or sandbox with review and rollback available.","findings":"[SC2] unexpected: Installing Cursor is expected, but piping a remote installer directly into bash is not the least-risk or well-scoped installation mechanism.\n[TM2] unexpected: The shell pipeline is real artifact evidence and creates an unnecessary immediate-execution path for network content.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The workspace trust keystroke automation bypasses a user security decision instead of requiring review of the project and rule files.\n[EA5] expected: Model selection is a normal Cursor CLI feature and is disclosed as a user-invoked command, so this alone is not a Review concern.\n[EA2] expected: `--force` is a documented CLI capability, but using it in automation and CI increases risk without enough guidance about review boundaries.\n[PE2] expected: `sudo apt install tmux` is a normal package-install command for Ubuntu/Debian and is limited to installing tmux; it is not evidence of malicious privilege escalation.\n[T03] unexpected: The static scan's remote-installer concern is supported by the artifact text in both SKILL.md and README.md.\n[T05] unexpected: The static scan's workspace-trust concern is supported by the tmux automation that sends `a` after a fixed sleep.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015599641}}}}}